Step 7 — Apply REP-ASCA with permutation testing
With K_REMOVE fixed, rep_asca_applied() removes the repeatability subspace and runs the full ASCA with \(N\_PERM\) permutations. Permutation testing computes the null distribution of each effect’s sum-of-squares under random reassignment of factor labels, then derives a \(p\)-value as the proportion of permutations whose SSQ exceeds the observed value.

model = rep_asca_applied(X, d, L_err, K_REMOVE, nperm=N_PERM)

print("Model keys:", [k for k in model.keys() if not k.startswith('_')])

# Explore structure of the first effect to understand key names
effect_keys = [k for k in model.keys()
               if k.startswith('X') and k not in ('Xdata', 'XRes')]
if effect_keys:
    ek0 = effect_keys[0]
    print(f"\nKeys in model['{ek0}']:", list(model[ek0].keys()))
    sig_val = model[ek0].get('EffectSignif', None)
    print(f"  EffectSignif type : {type(sig_val)}")
    if isinstance(sig_val, dict):
        print(f"  EffectSignif keys : {list(sig_val.keys())}")
    else:
        print(f"  EffectSignif value: {sig_val}")

